assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/milestones/55","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/milestone/55","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/milestones/55/labels","id":5111549,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNTExMTU0OQ==","number":55,"title":"1.3.0.CR1","description":"","creator":{"login":"gsmet","id":1279749,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzk3NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1279749?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet","html_url":"https://github.com/gsmet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":306,"state":"closed","created_at":"2020-02-17T07:01:02Z","updated_at":"2020-04-07T16:29:53Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2020-03-06T01:45:27Z"},"comments":9,"created_at":"2020-02-28T16:59:46Z","updated_at":"2020-03-05T10:46:15Z","closed_at":"2020-03-05T10:08:52Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\r\nI have a method like this one:\r\n\r\n```java\r\npublic Set<MyDomainObject> getThingsCalled(String name)\r\n   return MyEntity.<MyEntity>find(\"name\", name).stream()\r\n      .map(entity -> entity.toDomainObject())\r\n      .collect(Collectors.toSet());\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen executed, the following warning is printed in the logs:\r\n\r\n```\r\n2020-02-28 17:14:37,005 WARN  [io.agr.pool] (pool-5-thread-5) Datasource '<default>': Closing open connection prior to commit\r\n2020-02-28 17:14:37,005 WARN  [io.agr.pool] (pool-5-thread-5) Datasource '<default>': JDBC resources leaked: 1 ResultSet(s) and 1 Statement(s)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf I change the method code to look like this:\r\n\r\n```java\r\npublic Set<MyDomainObject> getThingsCalled(String name)\r\n   List<MyEntity> entities = MyEntity.<MyEntity>find(\"name\", name).list();\r\n   return entities.stream() \r\n      .map(entity -> entity.toDomainObject())\r\n      .collect(Collectors.toSet());\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nthen there is no warning in the logs.\r\n\r\nJudging from the above, **it seams to me that the implementation of `stream()` method of `PanacheQuery<Entity>` does not handle DB resources properly**. According to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/5757#issuecomment-558531664 the issue started to appear after `1.0.0.CR1`\r\n\r\n### Environment\r\n - Java version:  1.8.0_172\r\n - Quarkus version: 1.2.1.Final\r\n - Build tool: Maven 3.6.2 \r\n\r\n### Additional context\r\nNot sure how relevant it is but the actual code runs on separate thread inside user managed transaction. The way the method is called looks more or less like this:\r\n\r\n```java\r\n@Inject protected TransactionManager tm;\r\n...\r\nexecutor().execute(() -> {\r\n   try {\r\n      tm.begin();\r\n      Set<MyDomainObject> result  = getThingsCalled(\"something\");\r\n      tm.commit();\r\n   } catch (Throwable e) {\r\n      rollback(tm);\r\n   } finally {\r\n      ...\r\n   }\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\nI wouldn't be surprised if the thread and transaction management contribute to the issue.\r\nThat said, I still believe there is a bug since `list()` method works fine (or so it seams) while `stream()` does not in the very same context.\r\n ","closed_by":{"login":"gsmet","id":1279749,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzk3NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1279749?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet","html_url":"https://github.com/gsmet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/7492/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/7492/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}